::ENG3_U02_L07_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.W.01] Narrative situation: A family restaurant is closing after thirty years. Nia grew up there and sees the closing as a loss. Tomas will open a community kitchen in the same space and sees the change as a new beginning. Which detail would best reveal Nia's perspective? {
~Tomas measures the room for new tables.#This reveals Tomas's planning, not Nia's loss.
=Nia traces the faded height marks on the kitchen doorway.#Correct. This detail shows personal memory connected to the restaurant.
~The street outside is busy.#This does not reveal Nia's perspective clearly.
~The building has a roof.#This detail is too general to show perspective.
}

::ENG3_U02_L07_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.W.01] Narrative situation: A family restaurant is closing after thirty years. Nia grew up there and sees the closing as a loss. Tomas will open a community kitchen in the same space and sees the change as a new beginning. Which detail would best reveal Tomas's perspective? {
~Nia folds an old menu into her backpack.#This reveals Nia's attachment, not Tomas's future plan.
~The chairs are stacked by the door.#This is neutral unless connected to a perspective.
~The cash register is unplugged.#This may show closing, but not Tomas's community vision.
=Tomas sketches where donated shelves and a soup counter could fit.#Correct. This detail shows his view of the space as useful for a new purpose.
}

::ENG3_U02_L07_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.W.01] Narrative situation: A family restaurant is closing after thirty years. Nia grew up there and sees the closing as a loss. Tomas will open a community kitchen in the same space and sees the change as a new beginning. Which structure would most clearly show both perspectives? {
~One paragraph that only lists facts about the building.#Facts alone do not establish perspective.
~A scene told only through Tomas's thoughts.#This leaves out Nia's perspective.
=A scene section from Nia's view followed by a clear shift to Tomas's view.#Correct. This structure helps readers follow both perspectives.
~A random list of memories with no character focus.#A list without focus can confuse the reader.
}

::ENG3_U02_L07_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.W.01] Narrative situation: A family restaurant is closing after thirty years. Nia grew up there and sees the closing as a loss. Tomas will open a community kitchen in the same space and sees the change as a new beginning. Which sentence uses figurative language to show Nia's view? {
~The restaurant was located on a corner.#This is factual but does not show Nia's view.
=To Nia, the empty dining room felt like a photo album with every picture removed.#Correct. The figurative language shows loss and memory.
~Tomas wrote a list of supplies.#This shows action but not Nia's perspective.
~The kitchen had two sinks.#This detail is neutral.
}

::ENG3_U02_L07_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.W.01] Narrative situation: A family restaurant is closing after thirty years. Nia grew up there and sees the closing as a loss. Tomas will open a community kitchen in the same space and sees the change as a new beginning. Which revision improves clarity in a multiple-perspective narrative? {
=Nia saw the empty room as an ending; Tomas saw the same room as a place where neighbors could gather again.#Correct. This revision clearly contrasts both perspectives.
~Nia was sad Tomas was hopeful things happened.#This is unclear and compressed.
~The room was old and new and everyone thought things.#This is vague.
~She saw it differently and he did too.#This does not explain the perspectives.
}
